+# Design — From History to Signal
+
+## Frame
+- 1920 × 1080, with a 120px content inset and a reserved lower footer zone.
+- Persistent upper-left module label and lower progress rail provide continuity.
+- One central visual idea per beat; no decorative clutter.
+
+## Type
+- Proxima Nova with the system fallback from `tokens.yml`.
+- Headlines use 72–96px, 900 weight. Supporting copy is at least 40px.
+- Small labels use 22px uppercase with generous tracking.
+
+## Color
+- Deep navy background and white/cultured cards.
+- Blue identifies structure and comparison.
+- Gold identifies evidence, results, and the forward direction.
+
+## Motion
+- A single paused GSAP timeline is the only animation clock.
+- Each scene enters through opacity and short vertical movement, then exits before the next beat.
+- The progress rail and signal path advance deterministically with the timeline.
+- No infinite animation, autoplay media, or non-seekable effects.
+
+## Accessibility
+- High contrast, large type, short on-screen phrases, and narration retained verbatim in scene metadata.
